# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, a file that git once classified as BINARY (because it briefly
# contained NUL bytes) keeps its CRLF verbatim through every later commit,
# because core.autocrlf skips binary files. docs/api-notes.md hit exactly that
# and ended up with \r\r\n on every line, which Python's universal-newline
# reader then expands into a blank line between every line of prose.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.zip   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.wav   binary
